WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.360
Speaker 1: Hey, you know, if you're wondering&nbsp;
what happened to all the crime since November 8th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:12.240
you're actually bringing up a very interesting&nbsp;
question. Fox News stories about violent crime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:19.800
are down 50% since the November 8th midterm&nbsp;
election. There's a very good research piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:27.120
from Media Matters Fox's coverage of violent crime&nbsp;
dropped after the midterms. Weekday violent crime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.280
segments decreased by 50% in the week of the&nbsp;
election compared to the weekly average since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:40.200
Labor Day. Are any of us surprised? In fact, Fox&nbsp;
News decreased stories about violent crime 63%.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:48.600
Media Matters has the details. This is not unique,&nbsp;
I assure you, to Fox News. We all knew in the lead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:54.060
up to the November 8th midterms that their stories&nbsp;
about violent crime, which of course ignore that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.740
By the way, stories about violent crime in what&nbsp;
they call Democrat cities not only ignore the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:05.340
facts of, for example, on a crime rate basis,&nbsp;
Oklahoma is more dangerous than New York state and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:11.340
on a crime rate basis. Both property and violent&nbsp;
crime. Oklahoma City is more dangerous than New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:15.300
York City. Remember rates a lot more. People&nbsp;
live in New York City. Aside from the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:21.120
it's an absurd narrative and that most cities&nbsp;
in general are run by Democrats because more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:25.860
Democrats tend to live in cities, we also know&nbsp;
that it's just a ploy. And I want to remind you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:31.380
I'm going to give you other examples, all of which&nbsp;
I have previously covered, because they do this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:38.580
all the time. In 2014, it was Ebola. Remember the&nbsp;
guy who went bowling at Brooklyn Bowl? And at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.480
time I was like at Brooklyn Bowl the day after and&nbsp;
I was worried that I get Ebola. What's going on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.880
anyway? 2014. We knew leading up to the midterms&nbsp;
that Ebola was being used by people like Rand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:53.460
Paul stands out and many others just to criticize&nbsp;
Barack Obama. That's all that it was. They just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.391
wanted to criticize Obama.
Speaker 3: Obama now.&nbsp;

00:01:55.391 --> 00:02:04.680
Speaker 1: And even though there were like. Four&nbsp;
cases and the one person that died got Ebola&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:10.080
outside of the country, if I recall. Correct. I&nbsp;
mean, it was crazy. And the day after the 2014&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.880
midterms, no more talk about Ebola. And it never&nbsp;
came back. They never talked about it again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:22.740
Another example, this is a classic, the migrant&nbsp;
caravan coverage. This one was in 2018 leading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:28.620
up to the 2018 midterms under Donald Trump. The&nbsp;
migrant caravans are on the way. They're coming.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:34.140
They're coming here. And we know that. Migrant&nbsp;
caravans tell us, oh, there's an election coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:41.220
up. And of course, as is reported here, migrant&nbsp;
caravan coverage plummeted after the midterms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:49.200
and indeed it did. And also a piece from Vox. Fox&nbsp;
News Barely Mentions Caravan. First morning after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.180
midterms, Fox and Friends had been just ranting&nbsp;
and ranting and ranting about caravans day after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:58.800
the midterms. They quite literally still have the&nbsp;
election results up on the screen. This was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:06.540
date. This was November. Sixth or seventh, 2018,&nbsp;
whenever, and they barely talk about it. We know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:11.700
the story. We know exactly what they do. It's very&nbsp;
clear at this point. Remember not to follow it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.960
and ask yourselves the question, not fall for&nbsp;
it. Ask yourself the question is this getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:20.280
coverage because it's important? Is this getting&nbsp;
coverage because it's accurate? Or is this getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:26.520
coverage because it serves a political goal or a&nbsp;
media goal which can often be creating fear and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.420
titillating and scaring viewers? If you ask those&nbsp;
questions, you figure these out pretty quickly.

